+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,11 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=20&cursor=<cursor>` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": ...}`:
+  returns up to `limit` items (an integer from 1 to 100, default 20), ordered
+  by `id`. Pass the returned `next_cursor` unchanged to fetch the next page;
+  it is `null` on the last page. Invalid limits and cursors return HTTP 400
+  with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
